Description: Bayesian dose finding for single-agent phase I trials with
    escalation with overdose control (EWOC; Babb, Rogatko and Zacks, 1998),
    using the reparameterized model in which clinicians give prior
    probabilities that the maximum tolerated dose lies below the minimum or
    above the maximum trial dose (Tighiouart and Rogatko, 2010
    <doi:10.1214/10-STS333>). Provides prior calibration, simulation of
    operating characteristics for discrete or continuous doses with
    toxicity-dependent feasibility bounds (Wheeler, Sweeting and Mander, 2017
    <doi:10.1002/sim.7280>) and safety and efficiency stopping rules, Trial
    Conduct workbooks with cohort-by-cohort dose recommendations, and an
    interactive 'shiny' application. Posterior computation uses 'JAGS'.
